<BaseLayout title="Visa Document Checklist: Preparation Planner for Pakistanis" description="Track visa preparation tasks and open the official checklist for your destination. Avoid treating a generic document list as a guarantee of completeness."><article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Visa Document Checklist Generator</h1><p class="mb-8">Choose a route and use the tasks to organise your work. Your official application checklist takes precedence over this planner.</p><DocumentChecklist client:load /><section class="prose max-w-none mt-10"><h2>Start with the actual requirements</h2><p>A document that was required for a friend may not be required for your application. Open the official link, answer the eligibility questions and save the checklist generated for your nationality, residence and travel purpose.</p><h2>Make each item traceable</h2><p>Keep a simple index linking each requirement to its file. Check the name, passport number, date range and legibility before upload. Use the authority’s current file-format and translation instructions; the planner does not invent a universal number of bank statements or salary slips.</p><h2>Ticking is a preparation aid</h2><p>Completing every task does not establish that the evidence is sufficient or that a visa will be issued. An officer may request more information. Do not create false records or bookings to complete a checklist.</p><h2>Save your own record</h2><p>Use Print to keep a preparation copy. Your ticks remain in this page’s browser state and reset on reload; we do not collect the documents. Never email us identity papers or bank statements to validate the list.</p><p>Next, check <a href="/tools/visa-fee-calculator/">official fee sources</a>, <a href="/tools/visa-processing-time/">processing information</a> and the relevant <a href="/guides/">guide</a>.</p></section></article></BaseLayout>
